  "grade": "artifacts:control-timers",
  "description": "The timer values' ranges (decision 5.36: the contract fixes each field and its range, never its value). Durations are integer milliseconds from 1 to 2^53-1, except keepalive_interval, whose 0 turns link_timeout off for a target, and connection_linger, whose 0 closes a connection with its last session (E0's value). Counts are integers from 1. The set travels whole: a timers command without one of the eight is refused. buffer_bytes is at least 1 and input_frame_max from 1 to 2^32-1. A connect without any of them stays schema-valid, so a v0.1 connect is valid at v0.2 — a v0.2 worker refuses it on its own rule, not the schema's.",
  "corpus": [
    "session model §11",
    "decision 5.36",
    "immortality §6.4"
  ],
